---
title: New MFA Device Registered Shortly After Help Desk Password Reset
id: 6b8c9d1e-2f3a-4b5c-d4e5-7f8a9b0c1d01
status: experimental
description: Detects a new MFA device or authenticator enrollment occurring within a short window of a password reset, a leading indicator of an in-progress account takeover via Scattered Spider's help desk impersonation vector.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-320a
    - https://www.huntress.com/threat-library/threat-actors/scattered-spider
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1656
    - attack.persistence
    - attack.t1098.005
logsource:
    category: application
    service: azuread
detection:
    selection_reset:
        OperationName: 'Reset password (self-service or admin)'
    selection_mfa_enroll:
        OperationName:
            - 'User registered security info'
            - 'Add registered owner to device'
    timeframe: 1h
    condition: selection_reset and selection_mfa_enroll
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate password reset and device re-enrollment during normal employee onboarding or device replacement
level: high

---
title: MFA Push Bombing - Repeated Authentication Prompts in Short Window
id: 6b8c9d1e-2f3a-4b5c-d4e5-7f8a9b0c1d02
status: experimental
description: Detects multiple MFA push notification failures or denials followed by an eventual approval for the same user within a short timeframe, consistent with Scattered Spider's push-bombing technique.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1621/
tags:
    - attack.credential_access
    - attack.t1621
logsource:
    category: application
    service: azuread
detection:
    selection_denied:
        ResultType: 'MFADenied'
    selection_approved:
        ResultType: 'Success'
        AuthMethod: 'MobileAppNotification'
    timeframe: 15m
    condition: selection_denied | count() by UserPrincipalName > 3 and selection_approved
falsepositives:
    - User experiencing genuine connectivity issues before successfully approving their own login
level: high

---
title: Signed Vulnerable Driver Loaded for EDR Impairment (BYOVD)
id: 6b8c9d1e-2f3a-4b5c-d4e5-7f8a9b0c1d03
status: experimental
description: Detects loading of a signed but known-vulnerable kernel driver, matching Scattered Spider's Bring Your Own Vulnerable Driver technique used to disable EDR/AV at the kernel level.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.huntress.com/threat-library/threat-actors/scattered-spider
tags:
    - attack.defense_evasion
    - attack.t1068
    - attack.t1562.001
logsource:
    category: driver_load
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        ImageLoaded|contains: 'KNOWN_VULNERABLE_DRIVER_HASH_LIST'  # populate from LOLDrivers or equivalent current feed
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate hardware vendor driver that happens to appear on a vulnerable-driver list but is pinned/patched
level: high

---
title: Cloud Identity Provider Enumeration Ahead of Privilege Escalation
id: 6b8c9d1e-2f3a-4b5c-d4e5-7f8a9b0c1d04
status: experimental
description: Detects bulk enumeration of users, roles, and admin groups across Okta, Azure AD, or AWS IAM within a short window from a single session, consistent with Scattered Spider's cloud/identity mapping stage.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1526/
tags:
    - attack.discovery
    - attack.t1526
    - attack.t1087.004
logsource:
    category: application
    service: cloud_audit
detection:
    selection:
        EventName:
            - 'ListUsers'
            - 'ListRoles'
            - 'ListGroups'
            - 'ListAdmins'
            - 'GetAccountSummary'
    condition: selection | count() by SourceIp, ActorId > 30
