---
title: Direct ESXi Hypervisor Encryption or Mass VM Shutdown
id: 6b8c9d1e-2f3a-4b5c-d4e5-7f8a9b0c1d08
status: experimental
description: Detects mass datastore file modification or a burst of VM power-off operations issued from vCenter/ESXi management, consistent with Scattered Spider encrypting the hypervisor layer directly to take down every hosted VM at once.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1486/
tags:
    - attack.impact
    - attack.t1486
logsource:
    category: application
    service: vmware_vcenter
detection:
    selection_poweroff:
        EventType: 'VmPoweredOffEvent'
    selection_datastore_write:
        EventType: 'DatastoreFileCopiedEvent'
        FileExtension|contains:
            - '.vmdk'
            - '.vmx'
    condition: (selection_poweroff | count() by SourceIp > 10) or selection_datastore_write
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate planned maintenance window with scripted mass VM shutdown
level: critical
